  "deviations": [
    "Brief variant is-media-left + is-multi-image (home/10-wellness) has the same layout as base; no combo classes are created for it. The only differences are real images and a heading-style-h3 heading.",
    "New modifier is-offset on image-trio-text_item for legal/11 and corporate/11 (staggered cards), not listed in the brief.",
    "No container-large: the is-left cards span 1520px of the 1600px frame (2.5rem side margins), wider than container-large (80rem). The plan uses padding-global (2rem) only, so cards are 1536px wide at 1600.",
    "Base trio bleeds past the viewport with vw units (list width 107.0625vw, gap 1.875vw) to keep the Figma crop of the outer images at every width; rem cannot express this.",
    "Header to cards gap on legal/11 is 56px in Figma; the plan uses the shared 2.5rem (40px).",
    "Section vertical padding uses padding-section-large (7rem). Figma shows about 120px above the wellness images, 40px above the dining images and about 166px above the legal heading; the gaps come from neighbouring sections, which page entries own.",
    "Bulleted lists use a Rich Text element (text-rich-text); nested list styling must be set in the Designer (MCP limitation).",
    "Card body text has no max-width: Figma's legal/03 text boxes are 378px inside 485px cards, but legal/11 lists use the full card width, and one Rich Text class cannot tell them apart without nested styling.",
    "Q020 build: the headingTag prop is not created (not a native prop type); the heading stays h2 and its size class is fixed per reference section.",
    "Q020 build: the is-left reference-section figures hold no img element, so the grey #D9D9D9 placeholder shows instead of Webflow's placeholder image.",
    "Q020 build: loading=\"lazy\" is left to Webflow's image default instead of a custom attribute; data-eager is set on the base images.",
    "Q020 build: the visibility props are boolean props bound to element visibility (paragraphVisible, ctaVisible, itemContentVisible).",
    "Q020 fix (Stephen, 2026-10-20): card titles use image-trio-text_item-heading alone, carrying the EYEBROW-CAPS values (heading font, 1.125rem, 1.2, -0.03em, lowercase), instead of the stack with text-style-eyebrow-caps. The Designer dropped that combo and rendered the titles at h3 tag size (2.5rem). The empty combo .image-trio-text_item-heading.text-style-eyebrow-caps is now unused."
  ],
